1
00:00:00,396 --> 00:00:06,540
In 1823, a London handbook told breeders exactly what a perfect game cock should look like.

2
00:00:07,836 --> 00:00:10,997
It was called The Game Cock, by a Distinguished Amateur.

3
00:00:10,997 --> 00:00:13,620
Price: one shilling and sixpence.

4
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:20,460
He traced the breed to the wild cock of India, and swore the dark reds were the hardiest of all.

5
00:00:21,756 --> 00:00:22,862
The ideal bird?

6
00:00:22,862 --> 00:00:24,497
Eyes sparkling with fire.

7
00:00:24,497 --> 00:00:25,542
A small head.

8
00:00:25,542 --> 00:00:26,684
A strong beak.

9
00:00:26,684 --> 00:00:27,730
A long neck.

10
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:28,859
Broad shoulders.

11
00:00:28,859 --> 00:00:31,236
The whole body shaped like a lengthened cone.

12
00:00:32,592 --> 00:00:36,667
Feathers short, stiff and glossy, lying close to the skin.

13
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:38,508
That was the mark of a sound bird.

14
00:00:39,816 --> 00:00:41,367
The colours most admired?

15
00:00:41,367 --> 00:00:44,468
The reds, with a black breast and a ginger wing.

16
00:00:44,468 --> 00:00:48,012
And the duckwings, with a bar of steel blue across the wing.

17
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:52,589
His breeding rules: never breed two old fowls.

18
00:00:52,589 --> 00:00:54,753
Three or four hens to one cock.

19
00:00:54,753 --> 00:00:56,964
Clean water, grass and gravel.

20
00:00:58,260 --> 00:01:01,914
Two hundred years on, breeders still judge by these points.

21
00:01:01,914 --> 00:01:04,476
Follow HOTCOCKER for more from the old books.

